WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.160
Infrastructure-as-Code gives teams a
repeatable way to define infrastructure in

2
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:11.577
files, review proposed changes, and apply
those changes through automation.

3
00:00:11.657 --> 00:00:17.479
That repeatability is powerful because it
makes infrastructure more consistent and

4
00:00:17.559 --> 00:00:19.176
easier to reason about.

5
00:00:19.256 --> 00:00:21.035
It also raises the stakes.

6
00:00:21.115 --> 00:00:24.026
An IaC workflow is not just documentation.

7
00:00:24.106 --> 00:00:27.422
It can create, modify, or remove real
resources.

8
00:00:27.502 --> 00:00:32.434
A small code change can affect networks,
identities, storage, compute,

9
00:00:32.514 --> 00:00:38.093
encryption, logging, monitoring, data
exposure, and production availability.

10
00:00:38.173 --> 00:00:43.349
A single module input or policy exception
may change who can access a system,

11
00:00:43.429 --> 00:00:46.582
whether storage is public, how traffic
flows,

12
00:00:46.662 --> 00:00:50.301
or whether a workload has the right
logging controls.

13
00:00:50.381 --> 00:00:55.232
The automation may be fast, but the impact
is still operationally real.

14
00:00:55.312 --> 00:00:59.841
IaC automation becomes part of the
infrastructure control plane.

15
00:00:59.921 --> 00:01:05.662
Repositories, pull requests, branch
protection, pipeline runners, credentials,

16
00:01:05.742 --> 00:01:08.815
state backends, modules, providers, plans,

17
00:01:08.895 --> 00:01:13.423
and approval gates all influence what
happens in the environment.

18
00:01:13.503 --> 00:01:15.201
If those pieces are weak,

19
00:01:15.281 --> 00:01:20.860
an organization can have beautifully
written infrastructure code and still make

20
00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.072
unsafe changes.

21
00:01:22.152 --> 00:01:27.085
Secure IaC automation means making
infrastructure change controlled,

22
00:01:27.165 --> 00:01:30.561
reviewed, scoped, observable, and
recoverable.

23
00:01:30.641 --> 00:01:34.603
The objective is not to slow every team
down with friction.

24
00:01:34.683 --> 00:01:39.535
The objective is to build a path where the
right change can move quickly,

25
00:01:39.615 --> 00:01:44.143
with the right identity, the right
evidence, the right approvals,

26
00:01:44.223 --> 00:01:47.700
and a clear way to detect and recover from
mistakes.
